        "original_id": "d0fa1451-5361-5653-9d68-612bd13fb4c4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Seven Seas to Calais\n- People: Rudolph Maté, Primo Zeglio, Sir Francis Drake\n- Topics: Italian adventure films, Elizabethan-era privateering\n\nFacts:\n- Sir Francis Drake was born around 1540 and died on 28 January 1596.\n- Sir Francis Drake was an English sea captain and privateer of the Elizabethan era.\n- Seven Seas to Calais is a 1962 Italian adventure film made in Eastmancolor and CinemaScope.\n- Seven Seas to Calais was directed by Rudolph Maté and Primo Zeglio.\n- Seven Seas to Calais was Rudolph Maté’s final film.\n- Seven Seas to Calais depicts the career of Sir Francis Drake.",
